n3.12/dist-packages/torch/lib/../../nvidia/cu13/lib/libcublas.so.13 (0x00007f6f8dc00000)\n\tlibcublasLt.so.13 => /usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/torch/lib/../../nvidia/cu13/lib/libcublasLt.so.13 (0x00007f6f67c00000)\n\tlibutil.so.1 => /usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libutil.so.1 (0x00007f6fcfe21000)\n\tlibnvshmem_host.so.3 => /usr/local/lib/python3.12/dist-packages/torch/lib/../../nvidia/nvshmem/lib/libnvshmem_host.so.3 (0x00007f6f5de00000)\n\tlibnvJitLink.so.13 => /usr/local/cuda/lib64/libnvJitLink.so.13 (0x00007f6f57ebd000)\n", "stderr": ""}, "help": {"returncode": 0, "stdout": "REQUIRED OPTIONS:\n  --model <PATH>: Path to the model directory. This is the only required flag.\n\nHELP OPTIONS:\n  -h, --help: Display this help message and exit.\n\nCONFIG OPTIONS:\n  --config_json_file: Path to a JSON config file. Values in the file override command-line flag values.\n  --enable_dump_config_json: Whether to dump the resolved startup config as JSON.\n  --dump_config_json_file: Path to write the resolved startup config as JSON. Used only when enable_dump_config_json is true.\n\nSERVICE OPTIONS:\n  --host: Host name for brpc server.\n  --port: Port for brpc server.\n  --rpc_idle_timeout_s: Connection will be closed if there is no read/write operations during the last `rpc_idle_timeout_s`. -1 means wait indefinitely.\n  --rpc_channel_timeout_ms: Max duration of bRPC Channel. -1 means wait indefinitely.\n  --max_reconnect_count: The max count for worker try to connect to server.\n  --num_threads: Number of threads to process requests.\n  --max_concurrent_requests: Maximum number of concurrent requests the xllm service can handle. If set to 0, there is no limit.\n  --num_request_handling_threads: Number of threads for handling input requests.\n  --num_response_handling_threads: Number of threads for handling responses.\n  --health_check_interval_ms: Worker health check interval in milliseconds.\n  --enable_json_object_output: Enable response_format json_object constrained decoding. When disabled, json_object requests are accepted without applying JSON grammar constraints.\n  --enable_verbose_trace_log: Enable asynchronous verbose request-trace logging to a file. When enabled, request and response trace events are written off the serving hot path by a background thread.\n  --verbose_trace_log_path: Base file path for the verbose request-trace log. When nnodes is greater than 1, _rank_<node_rank> is inserted before the final extension (for example, log/verbose_trace_rank_2.log). Single-rank serving uses this path unchanged. Used only when verbose trace logging is enabled. Defaults to log/verbose_trace.log, so it sits alongside node_<rank>.log.\n  --verbose_trace_log_max_size_mb: Max size in MiB of a single verbose request-trace log file before it is rotated. Defaults to 1024 (1 GiB).\n  --verbose_trace_log_max_files: Max number of verbose request-trace log files to keep per rank, including the active file. Each rank rotates independently and removes its oldest file once this many exist; this is not a deployment-wide limit. Defaults to 1000.\n\nMODEL OPTIONS:\n  --model_id: hf model name.\n  --model: Name or path of the huggingface model to use.\n  --model_impl: Model executor implementation. Empty/'native' uses the built-in C++ model; 'python' runs the graph via the embedded Python interpreter ('python' model package).\n  --backend: Choose the backend model type. 'llm' for text-only, 'vlm' for multimodal (text and images), 'dit' for diffusion models.\n  --task: The task to use the model for(e.g. generate, embed, mm_embed).\n  --python_model_path: Filesystem directory that contains the 'xllm' package, prepended to sys.path so the embedded interpreter can import the 'xllm.python' model executor subpackage. Falls back to the XLLM_PYTHON_MODEL_PATH env var when empty.\n  --limit_image_per_prompt: Maximum number of image per prompt. Only applicable for multimodal models.\n  --max_encoder_cache_size: Max gpu/npu memory size in MB for encoder cache per worker. Default is 0, which disables encoder cache.\n  --max_processor_cache_items: Maximum number of multimodal processor results cached on the master. Capacity is counted by item. Default is 256; set to 0 to disable processor cache.\n  --reasoning_parser: Specify the reasoning parser for handling reasoning interactions(e.g. auto, glm45, glm47, glm5, qwen3, qwen35, deepseek-r1).\n  --tool_call_parser: Specify the parser for handling tool-call interactions(e.g. auto, qwen25, qwen3, qwen35, qwen3_coder, kimi_k2, deepseekv3, deepseekv32, deepseekv4, glm45, glm47, glm5).\n  --enable_qwen3_reranker: Whether to enable qwen3 reranker.\n  --enable_return_mm_full_embeddings: return vit and sequence embeddings for vlm models\n  --mm_download_headers: Service-level default HTTP headers for multimodal downloads, as a JSON object. Per-request headers take precedence. Example: '{\"Authorization\":\"Bearer xxx\"}'\n  --flashinfer_workspace_buffer_size: The user reserved workspace buffer used to store intermediate attention results in split-k algorithm for flashinfer.\n  --use_audio_in_video: Whether to decode both audio and video when the input is a video.\n  --use_cpp_chat_template: Use native C++ chat template for supported models (e.g. deepseek_v32, deepseek_v4) instead of Jinja. Set to false to fallback to Jinja for debugging.\n\nLOAD OPTIONS:\n  --enable_manual_loader: Pin decoder layer weights to host memory and use async H2D transfer. Required by enable_rolling_load; also implied by enable_xtensor.\n  --enable_rolling_load: Enable rolling weight load: keep only N decoder layer weight slots in HBM and stream-load each layer just-in-time. Requires enable_manual_loader=true. NPU only.\n  --rolling_load_num_cached_layers: Number of decoder layer weight slots to keep in HBM when enable_rolling_load=true.\n  --rolling_load_num_rolling_slots: Number of rolling slots used by decoder rolling load. Fixed slots are computed as rolling_load_num_cached_layers - rolling_load_num_rolling_slots. -1 means auto (min(2, preload_count)). Must be in [-1, rolling_load_num_cached_layers].\n  --enable_prefetch_weight: Whether to enable prefetch weight,only applicable to Qwen3-dense model.The default prefetching ratio for gateup weight is 40%.If adjustments are needed, e.g. export PREFETCH_COEFFOCIENT=0.5\n\nKV CACHE OPTIONS:\n  --block_size: Number of slots per kv cache block. Default is 128.\n  --max_cache_size: Max gpu memory size for kv cache. Default is 0, which means cache size is calculated by available memory.\n  --max_memory_utilization: The fraction of GPU memory to be used for model inference, including model weights and kv cache.\n  --kv_cache_dtype: KV cache data type for quantization. \"auto\" (default): KV cache dtype aligns with model dtype (no quantization). MLU supports int8. CUDA Python eager supports experimental int8, fp8 (alias for fp8_e4m3), fp8_e4m3, fp8_e5m2 and packed int4. Native FlashInfer supports FP8 E4M3 and block-scaled NVFP4 resident pages, including hybrid linear-state models and decode CUDA Graph. Mixed modes bf16_int8, bf16_fp8_e4m3 and bf16_int4 keep K in BF16 and compress only V. CUDA attention uses fused Triton kernels in Python eager.\n  --kv_cache_backend: KV attention backend: auto preserves platform defaults; flashinfer selects native paged BF16/FP8 E4M3/NVFP4 on CUDA; reference selects the eager reference implementation.\n  --kv_cache_k_scale: Positive FP32-representable global K decode scale for native low-precision KV.\n  --kv_cache_v_scale: Positive FP32-representable global V decode scale for native low-precision KV.\n  --kv_cache_prefill_backend: Native FlashInfer prefill: auto selects FA3 for unquantized SM90 KV and FA2 otherwise; fa2/fa3 select explicitly. Low-precision KV with BF16 queries requires FA2.\n  --kv_cache_decode_backend: Native FlashInfer decode: auto/flashinfer use paged decode; xqa selects XQA explicitly. NVFP4 requires flashinfer.\n  --indexer_cache_dtype: Indexer cache data type for quantization. \"auto\" (default): Indexer cache dtype aligns with model dtype (no quantization). \"int8\": Enables INT8 quantization when supported. Supported on NPU and MLU backends.\n  --enable_prefix_cache: Whether to enable the prefix cache for the block manager.\n  --enable_in_batch_prefix_cache: Whether to cache admitted prefill full blocks into the prefix cache so that later requests in the same batch can share them.\n  --max_linear_state_cache_slots: Maximum active linear-attention state cache slots. 0 derives an automatic capacity from the available KV cache budget.\n  --xxh3_128bits_seed: Default XXH3 128-bits hash seed.\n  --enable_xtensor: Whether to enable xtensor for model weights with physical page pool.\n  --phy_page_granularity_size: Granularity size for one physical page in bytes, default 2MB, when enable continuous kv cache.\n\nKV CACHE STORE OPTIONS:\n  --prefetch_timeout: Stop issuing new KV cache Store prefetch batches after this timeout; wait for in-flight batches before admission.\n  --prefetch_batch_size: Prefetch from kvcache store copy batch size.\n  --layers_wise_copy_batchs: Layer wise H2D copy batchs.\n  --host_blocks_factor: Host block factor, e.g. host block num = host_blocks_factor * hbm block num.\n  --enable_kvcache_store: Whether to use kvcache store.\n  --store_protocol: KV cache store protocol(e.g. tcp, rdma).\n  --store_rdma_devices: Comma-separated RDMA HCAs for the embedded Store client.\n  --store_master_server_address: The Store master address: IP:Port for standalone mode or etcd://IP:Port;IP:Port;... for high availability mode.\n  --store_metadata_server: The address of the kv cache store metadata service.\n  --store_local_hostname: The local host name of the kv cache store client.\n  --enable_control_h2d_block_num: Whether to control h2d copy block num.\n\nBEAM SEARCH OPTIONS:\n  --enable_beam_search_kernel: Whether to enable beam search kernel.\n  --beam_width: Beam width for beam search.\n  --enable_block_copy_kernel: Whether to use block copy kernel on supported backends.\n  --enable_topk_sorted: Whether to enable sorted output for topk.\n\nSCHEDULER OPTIONS:\n  --max_tokens_per_batch: Max number of tokens per batch.\n  --max_seqs_per_batch: Max number of sequences per batch.\n  --enable_schedule_overlap: Whether to enable schedule overlap.\n  --prefill_scheduling_memory_usage_threshold: The memory usage threshold during prefill scheduling.\n  --enable_chunked_prefill: Whether to enable chunked prefill.\n  --max_tokens_per_chunk_for_prefill: Max number of token per chunk in prefill stage.\n  --chunked_match_frequency: Number of sequence prefix cache match frequency.\n  --use_zero_evict: Use ZeroEvictionScheduler but ContinuousScheduler.\n  --max_decode_token_per_sequence: Max decode token per sequence which used for ZeroEvictionScheduler.\n  --priority_strategy: Priority strategy for requests(e.g. fcfs, priority, deadline).\n  --enable_mix_batch: Enable mixed batch (prefill + decode in same batch). Forced to false when CP or MTP is active.\n  --enable_online_preempt_offline: Whether to enable online preempt offline.\n  --aggressive_coeff: Aggressive coefficient for MixScheduler urgency judgment.\n  --starve_threshold: Starvation threshold coefficient for MixScheduler.\n  --enable_starve_prevent: Whether to enable anti-starvation in MixScheduler.\n  --enable_dp_fair_token_budget: Fair per-DP-group token budget for prefill scheduling on disagg PD PREFILL instances. Caps each DP group at max_tokens_per_batch / dp_size tokens per scheduling round.\n\nPARALLEL OPTIONS:\n  --dp_size: Data parallel size for MLA attention.\n  --ep_size: Expert parallel size for MoE model.\n  --cp_size: Context parallel size for DSA attention.\n  --layerwise_split_size: Layer-owner KV cache group size inside each attention TP group. 1 disables layerwise split; values > 1 shard persistent KV by layer owner and enable layerwise-split communication. The value must divide attention TP size.\n  --kv_split_size: KV-cache split width. 0 falls back to cp_size (legacy); 1 means no KV split (each CP rank stores full KV, skips prefix AllGather); other K (K divides cp_size) means KV is sharded across K ranks while token-CP still uses cp_size.\n  --tp_size: Tensor parallelism size, only used for DiT model.\n  --sp_size: Sequence parallelism size, only used for DiT model.\n  --cfg_size: Classifier-free guidiance parallelism size, only used for DiT model.\n  --vae_size: Vae patch parallelism size\n  --text_encoder_tp_size: Text encoder tensor parallelism size for DiT model.\n  --communication_backend: NPU communication backend.(e.g. lccl, hccl). When enable dp, use hccl.\n  --enable_mm_encoder_dp: Enable encoder data parallelism for multi-modal models.\n  --enable_multi_stream_parallel: Whether to enable computation communication parallel by two streams and two micro batches in prefill stage.\n  --micro_batch_num: Default use two micro batches for multi-stream parallel.\n  --enable_dp_balance: Whether to enable dp load balance, if true, sequences within a single dp batch will be shuffled.\n\nEP LOAD BALANCE OPTIONS:\n  --enable_eplb: Whether to use expert parallel load balance.\n  --redundant_experts_num: Number of redundant experts on per device.\n  --eplb_update_interval: EPLB update rate.\n  --eplb_min_peak_load_improvement: Minimum peak-rank load reduction required before any EPLB policy publishes a new placement. Must be in [0, 1].\n  --eplb_policy_kind: EPLB rebalance policy kind: 'balanced' (default) or 'greedy'. Historical policy names remain accepted as compatibility aliases. Unknown values silently fall back to 'greedy'.\n  --eplb_use_decode_only_load: When true, only real decode tokens contribute to expert_load; prefill rows in mixed batches and graph padding are filtered. Off by default so behavior is unchanged unless operators opt in.\n  --eplb_prepare_timeout_seconds: Manager-thread backstop timeout in seconds when devices fail to report a layer prepared (worker crash mid-prepare, weight provider unwired). After this many seconds waiting on the same layer, the manager warns and skips to the next layer so the rebalance loop keeps progressing.\n  --expert_parallel_degree: Expert parallel degree.\n  --rank_tablefile: ATB HCCL rank table file.\n\nDISTRIBUTED OPTIONS:\n  --master_node_addr: The master address for multi-node distributed serving(e.g. 10.18.1.1:9999).\n  --xtensor_master_node_addr: The master address for XTensor distributed service(e.g. 10.18.1.1:9999).\n  --nnodes: The number of multi-nodes.\n  --node_rank: The node rank.\n  --etcd_addr: Etcd address for save instance meta info.\n  --etcd_namespace: Optional etcd namespace prefix for all xllm keys, e.g. prod-a.\n  --enable_service_routing: Whether to use xllm service routing.\n  --heart_beat_interval: Heart beat interval.\n  --etcd_ttl: Time to live for etcd.\n\nDISAGGREGATED PREFILL-DECODE OPTIONS:\n  --enable_disagg_pd: Whether to enable disaggregated prefill and decode execution.\n  --enable_pd_ooc: Whether to enable online-offline co-location in disaggregated PD mode.\n  --disagg_pd_port: Port for brpc disagg pd server.\n  --instance_role: The role of instance(e.g. DEFAULT, PREFILL, DECODE, MIX).\n  --kv_cache_transfer_mode: The mode of kv cache transfer(e.g. PUSH, PULL).\n  --transfer_listen_port: The KVCacheTranfer listen port.\n\nSPECULATIVE OPTIONS:\n  --draft_model: draft hf model path to the model file.\n  --num_speculative_tokens: Number of speculative tokens.\n  --speculative_algorithm: Speculative decoding algorithm. Supported options: MTP, Eagle3, Suffix, DFlash, DFlash2 (NPU only), DSpark. Default is MTP.\n  --speculative_suffix_cache_max_depth: Maximum suffix tree depth for suffix speculative decoding.\n  --speculative_suffix_max_spec_factor: Suffix speculation max tokens factor relative to match length.\n  --speculative_suffix_max_spec_offset: Suffix speculation max tokens additive offset.\n  --speculative_suffix_min_token_prob: Minimum token probability used in suffix speculation.\n  --speculative_suffix_max_cached_requests: Maximum globally cached requests for suffix speculation (-1 unlimited, 0 disabled).\n  --speculative_suffix_use_tree_spec: Whether to use tree-based suffix speculation instead of path speculation.\n  --draft_sampling_mode: Draft proposal sampling mode: greedy or probabilistic.\n  --enable_mtp_draft_body_tp1: Whether to run the MTP draft body with tensor-parallel size 1 while keeping the draft LMHead on the target TP group.\n  --enable_atb_spec_kernel: Whether to use ATB speculative kernel.\n  --enable_adaptive_speculative_decode: Whether to enable adaptive speculative length for MTP decode.\n  --adaptive_speculative_min_gain: Minimum relative throughput gain required to include a draft token in adaptive speculative validation.\n\nPROFILE OPTIONS:\n  --enable_profile_step_time: Whether to enable profile step time.\n  --enable_profile_token_budget: Whether to enable profile token budget.\n  --enable_latency_aware_schedule: use predicted latency for latency aware schedule.\n  --profile_max_prompt_length: The max prompt length for profile.\n  --max_global_ttft_ms: all requests use single global ttft\n  --max_global_tpot_ms: all requests use single global ttft\n  --enable_profile_kv_blocks: true if generate kv cache for profile\n  --disable_ttft_profiling: Whether to disable TTFT profiling.\n  --enable_forward_interruption: Whether to enable forward interruption.\n  --enable_online_profile: Whether to enable the online timeline profiling endpoints (/start_profile and /stop_profile). CUDA only for now; pair with launching the server under nsys --capture-range=cudaProfilerApi.\n  --profile_backend: Online profiling backend: 1: 'torch' (default) records CPU+CUDA activities in-process and writes a Chrome trace on /stop_profile, no external profiler needed; 2: 'cuda' only toggles the CUDA profiler capture range and requires launching under nsys --capture-range=cudaProfilerApi.\n  --profile_dir: Directory the 'torch' online profiling backend writes timeline traces to. Empty means the current working directory.\n\nEXECUTION OPTIONS:\n  --enable_graph: Whether to enable graph execution for decode phase. When enabled, the engine uses graph mode (CUDA Graph for GPU, ACL Graph for NPU, MLU Graph, or DCU Graph) to optimize decode performance by reducing kernel launch overhead and device idle time.\n  --disable_graph_warmup: Whether to skip synthetic graph warmup during engine startup. When enabled, graphs are captured lazily by real requests.\n  --enable_graph_double_buffer: Whether to enable double-buffered ACL graph persistent params and graph instances for NPU schedule-overlap decode.\n  --enable_graph_mode_decode_no_padding: Whether to enable graph execution for decode phase without padding. If true, graph will be captured with every actual num tokens, as stride is 1.\n  --enable_prefill_piecewise_graph: Whether to enable piecewise graph execution for prefill phase when graph mode is enabled. When enabled, attention operations use eager mode while other operations are captured in device graphs.\n  --enable_graph_vmm_pool: Whether to enable VMM-backed graph memory pool for multi-shape graph memory reuse.\n  --max_tokens_for_graph_mode: Maximum number of tokens for graph execution. If 0, no limit is applied.\n  --acl_graph_decode_batch_size_limit: Decode batch size threshold for ACL graph on NPU. When actual decode batch_size > this value, ACL graph decode falls back to eager mode to avoid OOM.\n  --enable_shm: Whether to enable shared memory for executing model.\n  --use_contiguous_input_buffer: Whether to use contiguous device input buffer for executing model.\n  --input_shm_size: Input shared memory size, default is 1GB.\n  --output_shm_size: Output shared memory size, default is 128MB.\n  --random_seed: Random seed for random number generator.\n  --python_graph_backend: Graph backend for the Python model executor. Defaults to aclgraph on NPU when --enable_graph is enabled. Values: off (eager), cudagraphs (CUDA decode graph with eager prefill), aclgraph (NPU decode graph with eager prefill), or any torch.compile backend name.\n  --enable_fia_decode: Enable FIA for Qwen3.5 decode attention. Applies to both target and MTP draft models. Prefill attention is unaffected.\n\nDiT MODEL OPTIONS:\n  --max_requests_per_batch: Max number of request per batch.\n  --dit_cache_policy: The policy of dit cache(e.g. None, FBCache, TaylorSeer, FBCacheTaylorSeer, ResidualCache).\n  --dit_cache_warmup_steps: The number of warmup steps.\n  --dit_cache_n_derivatives: The number of derivatives to use in TaylorSeer.\n  --dit_cache_skip_interval_steps: The interval steps to skip for derivative calculation.\n  --dit_cache_residual_diff_threshold: The residual difference threshold for cache reuse.\n  --dit_cache_start_steps: The number of steps to skip at the start\n  --dit_cache_end_steps: The number of steps to skip at the end.\n  --dit_cache_start_blocks: The number of blocks to skip at the start.\n  --dit_cache_end_blocks: The number of blocks to skip at the end.\n  --dit_sp_communication_overlap: Communication & Computation overlap for sequence parallel\n  --dit_debug_print: whether print the debug info for dit models\n  --dit_laser_attention_enabled: whether to use the laser attention kernel (MindIE-SD, tuned for Wan2.2) in place of npu_fusion_attention for DiT attention.\n  --dit_generation_image_area_max: Maximum allowed image area (width * height) for image generation requests. If set to 0, there is no limit.\n  --dit_vae_image_size: Qwen Image Edit Plus VAE image size used to calculate dimensions.\n  --dit_enable_vae_tiling: whether enable vae tiling, currently only support qwen-image-edit-plus\n  --dit_sparse_attention_enabled: Enable block-wise sparse attention / RainFusion for WAN.\n  --dit_sparse_attention_sparsity: Sparse attention sparsity ratio in [0.0, 1.0). 0.0 = dense attention, 0.5 = drop 50 percent blocks.\n  --dit_sparse_attention_pool_size: Sparse attention pooling window size for block-wise mask generation.\n  --dit_sparse_attention_sparse_start_step: Sparse attention step index to start sparse attention. Steps before this use dense attention.\n  --dit_sparse_attention_version: Sparse attention version: 'rain_fusion' (frame-pairing + aclnnRainFusionAttention) or 'sparse_attention' (block-decompose + aclnnBlockSparseAttention).\n  --dit_sparse_attention_mask_refresh_steps: Sparse attention: recompute block sparse mask every N diffusion steps. 1 = every step (default), higher = reuse mask longer.\n  --max_sequence_length: Max sequence length for Flux2 text encoder tokenizer. 0 means disabled.\n\nREC OPTIONS:\n  --enable_rec_fast_sampler: Whether to enable RecSampler fast sampling path for Rec pipelines.\n  --enable_rec_prefill_only: Enable rec prefill-only mode (no decoder self-attention blocks allocation).\n  --enable_xattention_one_stage: Whether to force xattention one-stage decode for rec multi-round mode.\n  --max_decode_rounds: Maximum number of decode rounds for multi-step decoding. 0 means disabled.\n  --enable_constrained_decoding: Whether to enable constrained decoding, which is used to ensure that the output meets specific format or structural requirements through pre-defined rules.\n  --output_rec_logprobs: Whether to output rec multi-round token-aligned logprobs. When enabled, missing per-token logprobs are filled with the final beam logprob.\n  --enable_convert_tokens_to_item: Enable token ids conversion to item id in REC/OneRec response.\n  --enable_output_sku_logprobs: Enable REC / OneRec token-aligned logprobs tensor output.\n  --enable_extended_item_info: Enable REC extended item info parsing and output tensors.\n  --each_conversion_threshold: Maximum number of items emitted for each REC token triplet.\n  --total_conversion_threshold: Maximum total number of items emitted in one REC response.\n  --request_queue_size: The request queue size of the scheduler\n  --rec_worker_max_concurrency: Concurrency for rec worker parallel execution. Less than or equal to 1 means disable concurrent rec worker.\n\nFor more information and all available options, visit:\n  https://github.com/xLLM-AI/xllm/blob/main/xllm/core/framework/config/\nDocumentation: https://docs.xllm-ai.com/en/cli_reference/\n", "stderr": ""}}
